1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:04,760
Really quickly, I just want to talk to folks who consider themselves artists.

2
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:12,660
One of your key tenets as an artist is to protect other artists' work.

3
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:19,780
When you are involved in the creation of their work, you protect other artists' work.

4
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:23,980
What does protection mean? Protection means showing up.

5
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:29,480
Protection means when you can't show up, making sure that your role is covered.

6
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:34,440
Protection means not divulging any details that aren't supposed to be divulged.

7
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:41,940
Protection means giving your heart, not just your mind, to whatever role you have in that art.

8
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:49,120
When we talk about art, we're talking about things that are being created from the heart and mind, right?

9
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:53,860
And I don't think enough of us understand that and we need to self-check that.

10
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:58,180
Because sometimes we think we just have a job. No, you have a journey.

11
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:07,220
And when you are working with other people's art as a part of your journey, understand that each piece is stepping you forward.

12
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,680
Sometimes you find yourself in a position where you don't even like the person.

13
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:15,750
It doesn't matter. Art is bigger than you.

14
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:19,230
And even if you don't like that person, but you know that they are making art,

15
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:24,250
you have a responsibility to show up authentically and genuinely.

16
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:28,410
Yeah. So shout out to all my artisans out there.

